WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.200 --> 00:00:02.568
-Welcome back.
I'm here with Dakota Johnson.

00:00:02.568 --> 00:00:04.036
Dakota, you're not afraid
to tell it like it is,

00:00:04.036 --> 00:00:06.072
so I thought that
we'd have some fun by asking you

00:00:06.072 --> 00:00:08.607
to settle some of
the biggest debates of all time.

00:00:08.607 --> 00:00:11.410
Are you ready for this?
-Yes.

00:00:11.410 --> 00:00:14.347
-It is time for
"Dakota Settles It."

00:00:14.347 --> 00:00:19.218 line:0%
-♪ Dakota settles it,
Dakota settles it ♪

00:00:19.218 --> 00:00:22.088 line:0%
-Alright.
-Wow. I love that.

00:00:22.088 --> 00:00:23.623 line:0%
-First issue...

00:00:23.623 --> 00:00:28.594 line:0%
Better rom-com -- "The Notebook"
or "When Harry Met Sally"?

00:00:28.594 --> 00:00:31.464 line:0%
-"When Harry Met Sally."
-I agree.

00:00:31.464 --> 00:00:32.865 line:0%
There you go. Next.

00:00:32.865 --> 00:00:36.302 line:0%
"Game of Thrones"
or "Lord of the Rings"?

00:00:36.302 --> 00:00:39.305 line:0%
-Oh, that's tough
because I feel like

00:00:39.305 --> 00:00:41.607 line:0%
people will be really angry
on either side,

00:00:41.607 --> 00:00:46.312 line:0%
but...I'm gonna say
"Lord of the Thrones."

00:00:46.312 --> 00:00:49.815 line:0%
-[ Laughs ] Oh, my gosh.
"Lord of the Thrones."

00:00:49.815 --> 00:00:51.183 line:0%
Oh, my gosh.

00:00:51.183 --> 00:00:56.088 line:0%
Next. Could Jack have fit
on the door with Rose?

00:00:56.088 --> 00:00:57.022 line:0%
-Yes!

00:00:57.022 --> 00:00:59.792 line:0%
Even if he was on top of her.

00:00:59.792 --> 00:01:01.394 line:0%
-[ Laughs ]

00:01:01.394 --> 00:01:03.963 line:0%
How would he get on top of her?

00:01:03.963 --> 00:01:05.631 line:0%
-What do you mean?

00:01:05.631 --> 00:01:08.500 line:0%
-I mean, you're -- you're
swimming for you life there.

00:01:08.500 --> 00:01:10.036 line:0%
It's freezing-cold water.

00:01:10.036 --> 00:01:13.439 line:0%
-Yeah, you just, like,
hoist up and slap on.

00:01:13.439 --> 00:01:17.543 line:0%
[ Laughter ]

00:01:17.543 --> 00:01:18.878 line:0%
-Here we go. Alright.

00:01:18.878 --> 00:01:22.749 line:0%
Is it "GIF" or "JIF"?

00:01:22.749 --> 00:01:25.151 line:0%
-It's GIF.

00:01:25.151 --> 00:01:28.020 line:0%
-It is JIF, but it's GIF.
You're right.

00:01:28.020 --> 00:01:29.188 line:0%
-It's GIF.

00:01:29.188 --> 00:01:31.624 line:0%
-But the guy who invented it
said it's JIF.

00:01:31.624 --> 00:01:33.326 line:0%
-Who's the guy who invented it?

00:01:33.326 --> 00:01:38.264 line:0%
-Uh, Fred...Jiffy...
uh, Mendelson.

00:01:38.264 --> 00:01:40.266 line:0%
[ Laughs ]

00:01:40.266 --> 00:01:42.535 line:0%
Alright, here we go.
"Sex and the City" question --

00:01:42.535 --> 00:01:46.172 line:0%
Should Carrie
have ended up with Big?

00:01:46.172 --> 00:01:47.373 line:0%
-No.

00:01:47.373 --> 00:01:48.407 line:0%
-Yeah, I agree.

00:01:48.407 --> 00:01:50.943 line:0%
It ended bittersweet and cool.

00:01:50.943 --> 00:01:53.012 line:0%
SJP's awesome. Perfect. I agree.

00:01:53.012 --> 00:01:54.847 line:0%
Great. Alright.
Take a look at this.

00:01:54.847 --> 00:01:57.784 line:0%
Is the dress blue and black
or white and gold?

00:01:59.685 --> 00:02:01.621 line:0%
-It's white and gold.
-Correct.

00:02:01.621 --> 00:02:03.722 line:0%
-But it actually sort of looks
blue and gold.

00:02:03.722 --> 00:02:06.058 line:0%
-It does a little bit.
It's like a light blue and gold.

00:02:06.058 --> 00:02:08.627 line:0%
-Yeah.
-I agree. It's neither one.

00:02:08.627 --> 00:02:10.196 line:0%
Trick question.
Alright, next up --

00:02:10.196 --> 00:02:13.733 line:0%
Team Jacob or Team Edward?

00:02:13.733 --> 00:02:17.070 line:0%
-Oh, um, Team Edward.

00:02:19.405 --> 00:02:21.474 line:0%
-Yeah, I think so too.

00:02:21.474 --> 00:02:26.546 line:0%
Next, how do you pronounce the
word at the bottom of my screen?

00:02:26.546 --> 00:02:28.414 line:0%
-"Cara-mell."

00:02:28.414 --> 00:02:29.916 line:0%
-Yeah.

00:02:29.916 --> 00:02:31.818 line:0%
You're classy,
'cause I would've said...

00:02:31.818 --> 00:02:34.620 line:0%
-We're not disagreeing on much.
-..."car-mell."

00:02:34.620 --> 00:02:36.789 line:0%
But --
-Do you say that?

00:02:36.789 --> 00:02:38.123 line:0%
-I think I say "car-mell."

00:02:38.123 --> 00:02:39.191 line:0%
"Car-mell"?

00:02:39.191 --> 00:02:40.760 line:0%
-"Cara-mell?"
-"Car-mell."

00:02:40.760 --> 00:02:44.030 line:0%
It's -- What I'm saying is
wrong. "Car-mell" corn.

00:02:44.030 --> 00:02:46.766 line:0%
"Cara-melled" --
"Car-melled" apples?

00:02:46.766 --> 00:02:49.501 line:0%
"Car-melled" app--
-"Cara-mell" apple.

00:02:49.501 --> 00:02:52.038 line:0%
-It sounds much better
when you say it.

00:02:52.038 --> 00:02:54.306 line:0%
"Car-mell" apple doesn't sound
like that. Yeah. Alright.

00:02:54.306 --> 00:02:57.009 line:0%
This next one, remember,
there are four to choose from --

00:02:57.009 --> 00:02:58.444 line:0%
best "Toy Story"?

00:02:58.444 --> 00:03:00.512 line:0%
I know the answer.

00:03:00.512 --> 00:03:04.684 line:0%
-Oh. Um, I like "Toy Story 3."

00:03:04.684 --> 00:03:05.852 line:0%
-That is correct.

00:03:05.852 --> 00:03:07.853 line:0%
That is the right answer.
-Is it?

00:03:07.853 --> 00:03:09.188 line:0%
-Yeah. It's definitely 3.

00:03:09.188 --> 00:03:10.690 line:0%
3 should've won
for Best Picture.

00:03:10.690 --> 00:03:13.426 line:0%
It's one of the best movies I've
ever seen in my entire lifetime.

00:03:13.426 --> 00:03:15.127 line:0%
-Yeah. I agree.

00:03:15.127 --> 00:03:18.064 line:0%
-Does cilantro taste like soap?

00:03:22.101 --> 00:03:24.770 line:0%
-No.
-Yeah. I agree.

00:03:24.770 --> 00:03:26.305 line:0%
-Oh.
-And finally,

00:03:26.305 --> 00:03:28.073 line:0%
one of the most debated
questions ever,

00:03:28.073 --> 00:03:31.043 line:0%
were Ross and Rachel on a break?

00:03:31.043 --> 00:03:32.077 line:0%
-Yes.

00:03:32.077 --> 00:03:34.247 line:0%
-They were!
I totally agree with you!

00:03:34.247 --> 00:03:36.949 line:0%
You heard it here first.
My thanks to Dakota Johnson.

00:03:36.949 --> 00:03:38.451 line:0%
Her new movie "Our Friend"

00:03:38.451 --> 00:03:40.386 line:0%
is in theaters
and on demand this Friday.

